ea  salt and black pepper and I give it a  stir then to another bowl I add some  melted butter some Frank's Red Hot Sauce  some minced garlic and some beaten eggs  and I give that a stir  and now it's time to bread I dip my  chicken tenders into the bowl of flour  and give them a nice coating then they  go into the Franks red hot sauce egg  mixture and then finally they get coated  in some panko breadcrumb place the  chicken tenders onto a lightly greased  baking sheet and set that aside next to  a ball I add some carrots and celery  with a little olive oil along with some  sea salt and black pepper then I give  that a good toss and I place them onto  the baking sheet with the chicken place  that into the oven at 425 degrees for  about 20 minutes until it's fully cooked  through I like to finish mine off with a  little drizzle of Greek ranch dressing  enjoy  for all of these meals I like to make a  big batch of my favorite green like rice  or quinoa and then divvy them up into  individual freezer containers to rewarm  throughout the week alright guys my  freezer is all packed and ready to go  with some awesome well-balanced meals I  hope you guys enjoyed this video if you  did be sure to give it the thumbs up  leave me a comment below with some of  your go-to freezer friendly batch meals  subscribe to the channel and I will see  you next time on Abbey's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

